body:
@sebitit Unfortunately, `@Nested` is (still) not supported. See #4393 for more details.

@stuartwdouglas In #4409 an explicit and descriptive exception was introduced for this case, but it was removed by the big classloader change: https://github.com/quarkusio/quarkus/commit/b67491c1ffe76248d5f01bc3e29be94c2cdd56a4#diff-985ca913dc620dcf2e54fd5e2b62a2bfL417
Do you remember why? Seems we should bringt it back...

Hi @stuartwdouglas ,

The issue still happen if the test class has multiple nested "Nested" classes.
I'm using quarkus version **1.11.0-final**

```
@QuarkusTest
@Tag("integration")
public class GreetingResourceTest {

    @Nested
    class NestedTestClass {

         @Nested
         class NestedDeeperTestClass {
         }
    }
}
```
